---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../../components/PageHeader.astro";
import WaitlistForm from "../../components/WaitlistForm.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Mentor Matchmaking: Coming Soon"
  description="A future platform connecting aspiring law readers with attorneys and judges open to sponsoring an apprenticeship. Join the waitlist as an apprentice or a sponsoring attorney."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Coming Soon"
    title="Connecting apprentices with sponsoring attorneys"
    subtitle="Finding a mentor willing to commit years of supervision is the biggest barrier to reading the law. We're building a platform to fix that."
  />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-navy">For aspiring apprentices</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-light">
          Search for attorneys and judges by state, practice area, and availability instead of cold-emailing
          your way through a network you don't have yet. Build a profile that shows you're serious.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-navy/10 bg-white p-6">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-lg font-bold text-navy">For sponsoring attorneys</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-light">
          Review candidates who already understand your state's requirements and the commitment involved,
          instead of starting from scratch every time someone asks you to consider mentoring them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-legal mt-12">
      <h2>What we're planning to build</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Searchable profiles</strong> for apprentices and sponsoring attorneys, filterable by state program, practice area, and time availability.</li>
        <li><strong>Structured onboarding</strong> that walks both sides through their specific state's requirements before they ever have a conversation, so nobody starts from zero.</li>
        <li><strong>Progress tracking tools</strong> to help apprentices and supervisors log required study hours and milestones together.</li>
        <li><strong>A vetting layer</strong> so apprentices can verify a prospective supervisor's bar status and experience, and attorneys can see a candidate's seriousness and prior preparation.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        None of this exists yet. This page is a placeholder for a real platform we're actively building.
        The fastest way to shape what we build is to tell us what you need below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <WaitlistForm />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
